    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 06/12/2006, the erection of a hip to gable development measuring 4.25m in width, and 2.99m high, and a rear dormer measuring 5.35m in width, 4.05m in depth, and 2.99m in height was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development lies within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the development would not exceed the 50m3 allowed for roof additions on semi-detached houses, and the development would not exceed 70m3 in total."
